---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import { currentSite } from '../../data/sites.mjs';
import { BRAND, LEGAL_POSITIONING } from '../../data/brand.mjs';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema.mjs';

/*
 * TODO: LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH
 *
 * Standard template, not reviewed by an attorney. Items to confirm:
 *   - That the no-brokerage language below matches the real estate licensing
 *     rules of every state in the network. This is the highest risk item on
 *     the site and should be reviewed state by state.
 *   - Limitation of liability wording and whether it is enforceable in the
 *     states we operate in.
 *   - Governing law and venue. Currently left unspecified on purpose, because
 *     naming the wrong one is worse than naming none.
 */

const site = currentSite();
const updated = 'July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`The terms that apply when you use this ${BRAND.name} website or send us information about your property.`}
  path="/terms"
  schemas={[
    breadcrumbSchema(site, [
      { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { label: 'Terms of Use', path: '/terms' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <div class="page section">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <Prose>
      <h2>About this site</h2>
      <p>
        This website is operated by {BRAND.name}. By using it, you agree to the
        terms below. If you do not agree with them, please do not use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>What we are, and what we are not</h2>
      <p>{LEGAL_POSITIONING}</p>
      <p>
        We buy land and we option land for our own account. We do not provide
        real estate services to you, we do not represent your interests in a
        transaction, and we are not paid a commission on anything. You are free
        to hire your own professional advisors at any point, and for a decision
        of this size you probably should.
      </p>

      <h2>Information on this site is general</h2>
      <p>
        The pages and articles here are written to help landowners understand a
        process most people go through only once. They are general information
        and are not legal, tax, financial, or engineering advice. Rules and
        programs change, and what applies to one property may not apply to
        another. Do not rely on this site as the basis for a decision without
        checking it with your own attorney or accountant.
      </p>

      <h2>No offer is made here</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is an offer to buy your property or a commitment of
        any kind. Any actual offer from us would come in writing, signed, and
        after a conversation. Submitting a form does not create an agreement
        between us and does not obligate either of us to do anything.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you send us</h2>
      <p>
        When you send us information, you confirm that you are permitted to
        share it and that it is accurate as far as you know. We understand that
        a landowner may not know the answer to every question, and that is fine.
        Saying you are not sure is always acceptable. Deliberately false
        information is not, since we make decisions and spend money based on
        what you tell us.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our privacy policy explains what we do with what you send.
      </p>

      <h2>Limits</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep this site accurate and available, but we do not
        guarantee that it is free of errors or that it will always be reachable.
        To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for losses arising from
        your use of the site or from reliance on general information published
        here.
      </p>

      <h2>Other sites</h2>
      <p>
        We link to outside sources, including utilities and government agencies,
        so you can check facts for yourself. We do not control those sites and
        are not responsible for their content.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. When we do, the date at the top of this page
        changes.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can go to
        <a href={`mailto:${BRAND.email}`}>{BRAND.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</Base>
